     "text": "On January third, 2009, Satoshi Nakamoto embedded a newspaper headline straight into code. You might think sending money always requires central banks verifying every single transaction. So Satoshi proved automated proof of work could cut out the middleman completely. Bitcoin launched to clear transactions without central bank approval, because the initial block encoded that exact bailout headline from The Times. Proof of Work solved that double-spending problem using a shared ledger, allowing anyone to transact without permission. Yet illicit crypto transactions hit roughly one hundred fifty-eight billion dollars in 2025, proving that decentralized code scales way beyond early banking experiments."
